Daemonarchy VirtIO DRM integration
=================================

patch-daemonarchy-virtio combines the existing generated LinuxKPI options fix
with the Linux 6.12 VirtIO DRM port from freebsd/drm-kmod PR #499 at
ae8fc4c421eb4c0d6d9e0821ea6b070e8aec8199. Upstream now reviews the restructured
6.13 implementation in PR #517; this integration keeps the release's 6.12.110
DRM core shared with its NVIDIA DRM companion.

Adaptations for 6.12.110 and FreeBSD CURRENT 1600027:
- Guard the current fbdev deferred-I/O code/label on Linux.
- Use base LinuxKPI's dma_sync_sgtable_for_device and vmemdup_user instead of
  the older compatibility definitions.
- Generate opt_linuxkpi.h and include common LinuxKPI configuration for VirtIO
  as well as the existing modules.

Imported Linux files retain their licenses; new FreeBSD glue retains MIT.
The source archive stays pinned to drm_v6.12.110_1. This patch adds no binary
objects, generated architecture links, private credentials or moving downloads.

Native amd64 testport passed stage QA, plist checks, install/deinstall and
package install/deinstall on the matching October 12 snapshot. An isolated
QEMU/KVM guest using the matching modules rendered Hyprland 0.56.2, accepted
keyboard/pointer input, switched resolution and rebooted into Hyprland again.
Final packaged-image and physical GPU regression qualification remain required.

Hyprland requires a VirGL-enabled host display (virtio-vga-gl or
virtio-gpu-gl-pci). The 2D-only device is not a supported Hyprland path.
Load virtio_gpu_drm during rc startup, never from loader.conf. Venus/Vulkan,
multi-head and module unloading are not qualified by these checks.
